{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>This one, etc.</b> They will be many, and most of them lovers of HaShem, to return to His house." "<b>And this one shall call by the name of Jacob.</b> To boast before the nations that he is of holy seed." "<b>And this one shall write on his hand.</b> Missing a bet, and likewise it is 'he shall write on his hand,' to come to the temple of HaShem." "<b>And surname himself.</b> Like 'and he shall call'; and the Rabbis interpreted it concerning converts, in the sense of 'and ten men shall take hold' (Zechariah 8:23)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {2 "The Hebrew text Ibn Ezra quotes reads יכתו (missing final ם), likely a manuscript abbreviation; resolved as 'he shall write.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:53.467286355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}